{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DkRQHMR1TrNTcYTaPCKZoZ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"title\":\"Decision\",\"permalink\":\"main/schemas/decision\",\"file_path\":\"schemas/Decision.md\",\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Decision\\ntype: schema\\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\\nentity: Decision\\nversion: 1\\nschema:\\n  decision: string, the choice that was made\\n  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\\n  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\\n  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\\n  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\\n  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\\n  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\\nsettings:\\n  validation: warn\\n  frontmatter:\\n    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision):\\n    - open\\n    - accepted\\n    - superseded\\n    - rejected\\n    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\\n    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\\n---\\n\\n# Decision\\n\\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\\n\\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\\n`bm_search(filters={\\\"type\\\": \\\"decision\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"})`.\\n\\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\\n\\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\\n\\n## Frontmatter\\n\\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\\nnever blocking.\\n\",\"frontmatter\":{\"title\":\"Decision\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"permalink\":\"main/schemas/decision\",\"entity\":\"Decision\",\"version\":1,\"schema\":{\"decision\":\"string, the choice that was made\",\"rationale?\":\"string, why this choice over the alternatives\",\"alternative?(array)\":\"string, options that were considered and not taken\",\"consequence?(array)\":\"string, what this decision commits us to\",\"context?\":\"string, the situation that prompted the decision\",\"affects?(array)\":\"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\",\"supersedes?\":\"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\"},\"settings\":{\"validation\":\"warn\",\"frontmatter\":{\"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)\":[\"open\",\"accepted\",\"superseded\",\"rejected\"],\"decided?\":\"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\",\"project?\":\"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\"}}},\"checksum\":\"bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cf0cc651-05da-4541-be27-68bb809df671","uuid":"f9ec63ff-8caa-49bb-b5ea-849f9409baed","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:37:59.450Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"title\":\"Decision\",\"permalink\":\"main/schemas/decision\",\"file_path\":\"schemas/Decision.md\",\"content\":\"---\\ntitle: Decision\\ntype: schema\\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\\nentity: Decision\\nversion: 1\\nschema:\\n  decision: string, the choice that was made\\n  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\\n  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\\n  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\\n  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\\n  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\\n  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\\nsettings:\\n  validation: warn\\n  frontmatter:\\n    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision):\\n    - open\\n    - accepted\\n    - superseded\\n    - rejected\\n    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\\n    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\\n---\\n\\n# Decision\\n\\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\\n\\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\\n`bm_search(filters={\\\"type\\\": \\\"decision\\\", \\\"status\\\": \\\"open\\\"})`.\\n\\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\\n\\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\\n\\n## Frontmatter\\n\\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\\nnever blocking.\\n\",\"frontmatter\":{\"title\":\"Decision\",\"type\":\"schema\",\"permalink\":\"main/schemas/decision\",\"entity\":\"Decision\",\"version\":1,\"schema\":{\"decision\":\"string, the choice that was made\",\"rationale?\":\"string, why this choice over the alternatives\",\"alternative?(array)\":\"string, options that were considered and not taken\",\"consequence?(array)\":\"string, what this decision commits us to\",\"context?\":\"string, the situation that prompted the decision\",\"affects?(array)\":\"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\",\"supersedes?\":\"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\"},\"settings\":{\"validation\":\"warn\",\"frontmatter\":{\"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)\":[\"open\",\"accepted\",\"superseded\",\"rejected\"],\"decided?\":\"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\",\"project?\":\"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\"}}},\"checksum\":\"bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96\"}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"Basic Memory","version":"4.1.3"}},"structuredContent":{"title":"Decision","permalink":"main/schemas/decision","file_path":"schemas/Decision.md","content":"---\ntitle: Decision\ntype: schema\npermalink: main/schemas/decision\nentity: Decision\nversion: 1\nschema:\n  decision: string, the choice that was made\n  rationale?: string, why this choice over the alternatives\n  alternative?(array): string, options that were considered and not taken\n  consequence?(array): string, what this decision commits us to\n  context?: string, the situation that prompted the decision\n  affects?(array): Entity, work or notes this decision bears on\n  supersedes?: Entity, a prior decision this one replaces\nsettings:\n  validation: warn\n  frontmatter:\n    status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision):\n    - open\n    - accepted\n    - superseded\n    - rejected\n    decided?: string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)\n    project?: string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to\n---\n\n# Decision\n\nA **DecisionNote** is a durable record of a real choice — one with alternatives\nand a rationale, not a passing preference. Basic Memory host integrations\nencourage agents to capture these as decisions are made or explicitly requested.\n\nDecisions are found by structured recall:\n`bm_search(filters={\"type\": \"decision\", \"status\": \"open\"})`.\n\n## What makes a good DecisionNote\n\n- **decision** — state the choice plainly.\n- **rationale** + **alternative** — why this, and what was rejected. This is the\n  part that saves a future session from relitigating the same ground.\n- **consequence** — what the choice commits the work to.\n- **affects** / **supersedes** — relations that wire the decision into the graph.\n\n## Frontmatter\n\n`type: decision` plus `status` make decisions queryable. Capture decisions\nsparingly — one note per genuine decision, not per opinion. Validation is `warn`,\nnever blocking.\n","frontmatter":{"title":"Decision","type":"schema","permalink":"main/schemas/decision","entity":"Decision","version":1,"schema":{"decision":"string, the choice that was made","rationale?":"string, why this choice over the alternatives","alternative?(array)":"string, options that were considered and not taken","consequence?(array)":"string, what this decision commits us to","context?":"string, the situation that prompted the decision","affects?(array)":"Entity, work or notes this decision bears on","supersedes?":"Entity, a prior decision this one replaces"},"settings":{"validation":"warn","frontmatter":{"status?(enum, lifecycle of the decision)":["open","accepted","superseded","rejected"],"decided?":"string, when the decision was made (ISO timestamp)","project?":"string, the Basic Memory project this decision belongs to"}}},"checksum":"bd0b557fa5eb6c83f5db5373d420f221f4861912a4cb7a7c5eabd53d008cbe96"}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DkRQHMR1TrNTcYTaPCKZoZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
